  "premise_still_valid": true,
  "summary": "Draft PR #24407 (head 3777e26dc on d79dc4883) rewrites the domain:services 'this environment' strings in plugin-auth, plugin-security and service-settings under triage 6252585695's rule. 19 of the 20 sites in scope read 'this system' or drop the noun, and the three translated locales of the three settings keys change only the noun, to the ruling's own spellings (本系统 / このシステム / este sistema). Three strings the census missed, split across a concatenation in last-admin-guard.ts (:1516, :1612, :1619), were read and changed in place. One listed string is kept with its reason: auth-manager.ts:2527 (403 ENV_ACCESS_DENIED) exists only behind the cloud control plane's OIDC authorize gate and names the environment being signed in to from outside. Copy only: no status, code, key or shape moves, no test pins the changed noun, and all 67 derived gates plus the three packages' tests and typechecks are green.",
  "tests": "All under scripts/pm/os-verify-lock.sh (OS_VERIFY_LOCK_SLOT=os-dev-24368), at 3777e26dc. Build: turbo run build --filter=!@objectstack/docs --concurrency=2 → 'Tasks: 76 successful, 76 total' (3 cached), VERDICT command-exit 0. Tests (pnpm --filter PKG exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2): @objectstack/plugin-auth 'Test Files 163 passed (163) · Tests 3145 passed | 10 skipped (3155)'; @objectstack/plugin-security 'Test Files 187 passed (187) · Tests 3738 passed | 45 skipped (3783)'; @objectstack/service-settings 'Test Files 51 passed (51) · Tests 881 passed (881)'; each VERDICT command-exit 0. Typecheck (each package's own script, name echoed): service-settings tsc --noEmit exit 0; plugin-auth tsc + examples + check:test-typecheck '10 file(s) / 88 error(s) / 23 pinned signature(s) held' exit 0; plugin-security tsc + scripts + check:test-typecheck '0 file(s) / 0 error(s)' exit 0. eslint --no-inline-config over the 12 changed .ts files: exit 0, no output. No ablation: copy only, and the prose pins that exist (/recognises NO administrator/, 46 /last administrators?/i assertions, 'Self-registration is closed', the lock errors' class plus name/package/reason) all survive, so no pin moved and no new prose was copied into a test. test:repo not run locally (see deviations).",
  "gates": "Local: node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --commands --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack (no paths) derived 67 commands from the 13 changed paths at 3777e26dc (identical to the seat's lead list). All 67 ran after the final commit, exit codes captured before any pipe: 67 × exit 0. --ran: 'Run reconciliation — 67 derived, 67 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED, 0 UNRUN.' (a DERIVED zero). Selected verdict lines: check:i18n 'OK (10 package(s) — all bundles in sync …)' and check:i18n-stale-fill 'scanned 11 bundle set(s)', neither naming service-settings; check:doc-authoring '19057 customer-facing string(s) … clean'; check:nul-bytes 'OK (scanned 12249 text file(s) …)'; check-empty-changeset '1 declaring changeset(s) added'; check-adr-0087-registration 'this PR adds no declared-breaking changeset'. CI on #24407 head 3777e26dc, read once at 23:01Z: 37 check-runs. success: Check Documentation Links, Check PR Size, No other open PR may claim the same issue, No other open PR may claim the same single-writer path, Part-of PR must not also close its card, The card this PR closes must claim this branch, filter. skipped: Build Docs, Console Pin Gate, Dogfood Regression Gate (matrix), Dogfood Verify CLI, Packed-tarball smoke (opt-in), Temporal Conformance. in_progress (24), among them Build Core, Governed Surface Queue Guard, Test Core (1/6)–(6/6), Check Changeset, the seven Lint · lanes and the four Type Check · lanes. Not waited on.",
  "mcp_calls": "0 — no MCP GitHub tool was called",
  "api_writes": "2 relay strokes, each POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/dispatches (HTTP 204), executed as objectstack-fleet[bot]: (1) pr_create → POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/pulls (draft, #24407) + POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/24407/assignees (marchtian); read-back 17078 bytes sent = stored. (2) comment → POST /repos/objectstack-ai/objectstack/issues/24368/comments (this report). No label write (no skip-changeset: the diff publishes; the dispatch names no other label). Plus 2 git push (not REST): the empty-branch probe and 3777e26dc.",
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "auth-manager.ts:2527 ('You are not authorized to sign in to this environment.', 403 ENV_ACCESS_DENIED): the census counted it in-system and triage confirmed the census in bulk; this PR keeps it under the rule's keep-clause. Keep, or rewrite?",
      "options": [
        "A Keep it (this PR). Business need, measured: the only producer of the refusal is the cloud control plane's oidcAuthorizeGate (auth-manager.ts:726-735; unset in open editions and self-host, and nothing in this repo sets it outside a dogfood fixture), so the reader is a signed-in cloud user and the noun names the environment they asked to sign in to. Long-term fit: the same reading triage gave cli (the deployment addressed from outside, where the cloud noun is right). AI-error axis: no metadata or contract moves either way, so neutral. Startup focus: zero work.",
        "B Rewrite it to 'this system' or drop the noun. Business need: none measured, since no open deployment can emit it. Long-term fit: on the cloud's authorize page, 'this system' reads as the cloud itself, and the bare 'You are not authorized to sign in.' is wrong for an already signed-in subject, so either form is a less accurate message. AI-error axis: neutral. Startup focus: a one-line patch, no test reads the prose."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because the business-need axis is decisive: the string's only real reader is outside every running system the ruling covers, and both rewrites make the message wrong for that reader. The other three axes do not separate the options."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "carrier: #24406 · packages/spec/src/system/auth-config.zod.ts:401 carries the audience sentence ('Who may become a user of this environment's apps') as a TSDoc comment, which the census excluded as a comment. If #24406 reaches it, it should read as service-settings' audience help now does ('this system's apps') · noted, not filed",
    "carrier: repo:objectui pointer (triage 6252585695) · objectui 2ec9e2a apps/console/src/pages/auth/__tests__/registerRefusalCodes-10998.test.tsx:47-54 and packages/app-shell/src/console/auth/__tests__/registerRefusalCodes-11030.test.tsx:47-56 restate the old SELF_REGISTRATION_CLOSED / EMAIL_DOMAIN_NOT_ALLOWED server messages ('as the audience gate sends it') as fake-server fixtures. They are not parsers (the console maps by code in signUpRefusalMessages.ts), stay green, and are now out of date · noted, not filed",
    "carrier: none (承接者:无) · service-settings translations/en.ts has no settings.sms namespace, while zh-CN/ja-JP/es-ES do. English falls back to the manifest literal, and the coverage test checks only the three translated locales. An observation, not a defect · noted, not filed"
  ],
