  },
  "deviations": [
    "Three strings beyond the claim's list (last-admin-guard.ts:1516-1519, :1612-1613, :1619-1624; the census grep was blind to a phrase split across a concatenation) were changed in place under os-dev's bounded in-place rule: same defect class, mechanical with the rule fixing the shape, the file is already in the claim's surface and held by no other claim, the same gate family. This conflicts with the dispatch's 'Only the strings the claim lists', which I read as aimed at the other lanes' strings. I name the conflict here instead of choosing silently: the claim's string list was not amended (no write to the seat's claim), and the PR body lists them with the multiline-grep evidence. In the two refusals, 'administer the environment' in the same sentence moved too ('the environment', not the census phrase), so neither sentence names the system both ways. Revert is three lines if the seat disagrees.",
    "auth-manager.ts:2527 is kept, against the census's in-system class that triage confirmed in bulk. It is a per-string sense reading under the rule's keep-clause, the 'left with its reason' arm of the card's done-when, and it is carried in open_questions for the seat to rule.",
    "PM hypothesis falsified: check:i18n (10 packages) and check:i18n-stale-fill (11 bundle sets) walk only generated *.generated.ts bundle sets, and service-settings has no i18n-extract config, so its four hand-written locale files are outside both. Route taken, per the ruling's intent: noun-only substitution in zh-CN/ja-JP/es-ES, using the per-locale spellings the console's packs already carry under the same ruling (objectui PR 12959 / 12962), not a new translation.",
    "test:repo (vitest repo project) was not run locally: the diff changes none of its tests and the derived list does not name it. It belongs to CI's Test Core.",
    "Two git pushes against the budget's one 'git push' line: os-dev rule 1's empty-branch probe before any edit, then 3777e26dc.",
    "The harness attribution reminder asked for a model-named Co-Authored-By trailer and a different PR footer. The commit carries AGENTS.md's model-free pair (Claude-Session + Co-authored-by: Claude), and the PR body ends with AGENTS.md's session-URL footer, both as the repo's instructions and the dispatch require."
  ],
  "strings": [
