    },
    {
      "site": "packages/plugins/plugin-auth/src/auth-manager.ts:2527",
      "verdict": "kept",
      "reason": "403 ENV_ACCESS_DENIED fires only where the host sets oidcAuthorizeGate, which auth-manager.ts:726-735 documents as the cloud control plane's cloud-as-IdP hook ('Unset (open editions / self-host …) = allow'; nothing in this repo sets it but a dogfood fixture). The cloud, as OIDC provider, shows it to an already signed-in cloud user; the noun names the env client they asked to sign in to = the deployment addressed from outside, where triage keeps the cloud noun (its cli reason). 'this system' would read as the cloud itself; dropping the noun would tell a signed-in user they may not sign in."
    },
